## Purpose

Make the hosted dashboard trustworthy as a fleet-health surface by showing which installed client
and reporting instance produced each current snapshot, how fresh its evidence is, and whether
enrolled instances disagree. Local Tool Shed state and release tooling remain authoritative.

## Desired Outcome

An operator can distinguish healthy, stale, offline, quiescent, delivery-delayed,
behind-version, incompatible, unqualified, unknown-version, and divergent instances. Project
summaries name their source and freshness and never merge conflicting lifecycle snapshots.

## First Useful Boundary

- Extend the privacy-bounded schema-v3 report with controlled per-instance reporter health,
  semantic state digest, and release-provenance fields already known locally.
- Persist only bounded codes, versions, timestamps, digests, and counts on the hosted service.
- Derive release posture and divergence server-side with explicit unknown states.
- Render compact project-level trust indicators and a per-instance health table on the project
  health surface, refreshed through the existing semantic SSE revision.
- Implement and deploy the complete vertical slice through Work2; Work5 remains the formal release
  and production-reconciliation gate.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Reporter contract | Controlled health, release, and semantic-digest fields with strict privacy validation | existing schema-v3 reporter |
| Hosted truth | Per-instance persistence plus deterministic release/divergence projections | accepted bounded reports |
| Operator experience | Compact readable trust summary and per-instance drilldown | hosted truth |
| Qualification | Contract, ingestion, rendering, SSE, migration, deployment, and browser evidence | complete vertical slice |

## Readiness Gate Transfer

1. `G1-REPORTER-HEALTH-CONTRACT` requires bounded delivery, freshness, heartbeat, and quiescence
   fields while excluding paths, diagnostics, scheduler definitions, credentials, and free text.
2. `G2-RELEASE-PROVENANCE` requires installed, stable, candidate, and production-verified release
   concepts with controlled sources, timestamps, and explicit unknown handling.
3. `G3-INSTANCE-DIVERGENCE-UI` requires per-instance truth and deterministic divergence without
   merging conflicting local lifecycle snapshots or granting hosted mutation authority.

## Constraints

- Preserve each enrolled instance as an independent trusted source.
- Canonical version comparison must name its source and freshness; lookup failure is unknown.
- Reuse current report ingestion, models, semantic SSE, and authenticated dashboard surfaces.
- The hosted dashboard cannot update, restart, revoke, deploy, reconcile, or mutate local work.

## Non-Goals

- Remote repair, update, deployment, reconciliation, or credential operations.
- Raw outbox contents, repository paths or diffs, scheduler definitions, logs, or diagnostics.
- A modified-client status without a separate privacy-safe evidence contract.
- Silent selection of the freshest instance as project consensus.

